+vertices, including the first and last vertex. Section 4.1 proves that minimum
+undirected-Hausdorff simplification is NP-hard by reducing Hamiltonian cycle in
+segment-intersection graphs. Section 4.2 proves the analogous directed
+`P -> Q` result by reducing minimum line cover. These are worst-case reductions.
