+## Mechanical cost and compact route
+
+The numbers below are operation-count evaluations of the paper's displayed
+bounds, not timings of an unavailable geometry package.
+
+| candidate regime | shipping-size example | mechanical route | mechanical cost | compact/by-hand route | result |
+|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---|
+| proposed noisy-block plant | `n=128, k=8` | Imai–Iri all-pairs shortcut graph | `C(128,3) = 341,376` intermediate-point/segment checks, plus at most `8,128` graph links | 9 planted block boundaries when blocks are equal | fixed-block attack succeeds |
+| reverse directed Hausdorff | `n=128` | Section 4.3 valid-link construction | at most `128^4 = 268,435,456` primitive-scale steps | none supplied by the paper beyond identifying valid links | no Track-B compression target |
+| Fréchet | `n=32, k=4` | Section 5 dynamic program | `4*32^5 = 134,217,728` transition-scale steps | none for inverse-generated noisy blocks except doing the same link/matching tests | no compact route shorter than the mechanical decision work |
+| Section 3 Hausdorff counterexample | arbitrary `n` | generic optimization | polynomial/exponential depending on direction | fewer than 10 elementary choices: output `p_1`, any even-indexed vertex (so `p_2` works), and `p_n` | fixed-index attack succeeds |
