The proposed family fails the hardness gate after the Track B check. In the paper’s three-region construction (Theorem 1), a valid three-vertex simplification is read off directly—indeed any even-indexed middle vertex works—so the construction-aware algorithm and the “insight” route are both constant-size. For ordinary “plant a polyline and insert nearby points,” the strongest construction-aware method is the same linear scan needed by the compact route; increasing the scan past 300 operations would violate G9(c), not create a useful compression gap. The NP-hard reductions do not supply distributional hardness for planted Hamiltonian-cycle or point-line-cover instances. I’m documenting this as an H rejection on both tracks, with the paper’s exact theorem numbers and cost comparison.
